# llama.cpp prefills the 1014-token prompt fine (~1990 tok/s warm) but greedily samples an EOG
# token immediately, so decode is 0. Not a length threshold: the 543-token long-context-512
# prompt does the same, while short-chat's 12-token prompt generates 128 tokens at 37.5 tok/s.
# Suspected llama.cpp/Gemma-4 chat-template or special-token mismatch in the unsloth GGUF.
# Orthogonal to this comparison; decode is reported N/A rather than 0.
# Two real adapter bugs were fixed while finding this (both in LlamaCppRuntime):
#   - the KV cache was never cleared between generate() calls, so run 2+ of any --runs N task
#     died with "llama_decode (prefill) failed";
#   - the sampler chain was hardcoded to temp 0.7 / top-p 0.9, ignoring the task's greedy request.
